From 7f017d7df39f639f30e1a2f283ac123703b9ee85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 22:35:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: act on every configured symbol in the strategy runner

The per-symbol data loop ended before the decision, exit, kill-gate and
emission code, which ran once per outer loop. With several symbols only the
last one was acted on, and it could be managed with another symbol's price.
Handle one symbol per outer loop in turn so the existing code runs for the
symbol whose data was just read, and only with a price fetched in that same
turn; keep the startup flat check for every symbol on the first loop.
Single-symbol behaviour is unchanged.

Portfolio limits do not hold across symbols (pending entries are not counted
and percentage limits never bind); see the work log. Do not run a
multi-symbol campaign on this alone.

HIGH risk: READY_FOR_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW. Not pushed, not deployed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011p3WBrLHso7qjbJYsguxAY
