 # Review Stabilized Work Log
 
+## 2026-10-02 - Act on every configured symbol in the strategy runner
+
+- ENGINEER (Claude, separate thread), requested by the operator as the
+  backlog multi-symbol repair. Separate change on top of the cooldown,
+  protective-exit and reporting series; separate review.
+- Defect (Codex's review, on base and patched code): the per-symbol data loop
+  ended before the decision, exit, kill-gate and emission code, which ran once
+  per outer loop. With several symbols only the last one was acted on, and it
+  could be managed with a price left over from another symbol.
+- Change (+32/-3 in `strategy_runner.py`): each outer loop now handles one
+  symbol in turn, so the existing decision/exit/gate code always runs for the
+  symbol whose data was just read. With more than one symbol: the startup flat
+  check still covers every symbol on the first loop; a symbol is only managed
+  with a price fetched in that same turn (including one fetched during
+  warm-up); with no price this turn it is skipped and the fetch-failure
+  status stands. No price is cached between turns. The earlier isolated draft that moved the whole tail into
+  the loop (430 lines, 3 exit tests failing) is not used.
+- Single-symbol behaviour is intended to be unchanged: the new branches are
+  gated on more than one symbol. SHOWN: a 75-scenario single-symbol
+  differential (orders, per-loop gate results, final state) is identical
+  between the parent commit and this change.
+- Reviewer subagent returned ACCEPT_WITH_RISK and reproduced that a price
+  fetched during warm-up was discarded, so a held position lost its exit. Fixed
+  (price recorded where it is obtained) with tests in tick and public-OHLCV
+  modes.
+- Codex's local review of bundle rev10 then reproduced that the per-symbol
+  price cache reused an earlier price for exit evaluation after a failed
+  fetch, with no age check. Codex removed the cache in its isolated copy and
+  the operator accepted that correction. The cache is removed here to the same
+  description; this is Claude's re-implementation, NOT Codex's accepted bytes
+  (those live outside the shared folder), so it must be compared with them.
+  Two tests cover it: no exit evaluation on a failed fetch, and exit on the
+  recovered quote.
+- Pending-order exposure check (requested as the next safety check). SHOWN by
+  probe on this branch, three symbols all signalling buy, no fills:
+  with `max_concurrent_positions: 1` three buys are queued; with total and
+  strategy exposure limits near 0% and one symbol holding 100,000 notional,
+  the other two still queue buys. Cause, by reading: `summarize_exposure`
+  counts positions with qty > 0 only, `evaluate_entry` is called with
+  `open_intents_for_symbol=0`, and `list_positions` rows carry no exposure
+  fields, so the percentage limits never bind. NOT fixed here.
+- Consequences an operator must know before running several symbols:
+  each symbol is evaluated every N-th loop, so per-symbol cooldowns, tick
+  history and bar counters advance N times slower in wall time, and a symbol
+  whose fetch fails does not count down its cooldown that turn. Portfolio
+  limits do not hold across symbols (see the probe above). Do not run a
+  multi-symbol campaign until that is corrected and reviewed.
+- Not addressed (inherited): the `finally` block can persist one symbol's
+  last action under keys set for another symbol if an exception lands
+  mid-head; price persistence cadence has no test.
+- VERIFIED_ENV (cloud clone, Python 3.11.15): see commit message.
+- UNVERIFIED: Python 3.12, CI, hosts, a real multi-symbol campaign, auto venue
+  selection paths, exposure limits across symbols. No running campaign uses
+  more than one symbol today. HIGH risk. Not pushed, not deployed.
+  READY_FOR_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.
+
